# Hydri component & flow standards

Apply when creating, refactoring, fixing, or reusing components, screens, tokens, or product flows.

## UI & components

- Classify as **UI / styling / component architecture** (read `hydri-ui-architecture.mdc` + `AGENTS-UI-MOBILE-STANDARDS.md`).
- New paths: **kebab-case** only.
- New/touched component styles: **`.module.sass`** when safe — no broad global CSS; no `src/app/globals.scss` without explicit task.
- **Dumb components** — logic in hook/helper/domain/service inside the feature (or component folder).
- No business rules in `src/shared/` without reuse proof (Zero Redemoinho).
- Product tokens: **`Hy` / `hy-` / `--hy-*`** — no new `DSV2`, `dev-v2`, `lab-v2`, `legacy`, `old`, `new`, `tmp-*` in production.

## Architecture

- **Feature-based** — `src/app/` thin; domain/UI/hooks/mocks/tests in `src/features/`.
- SOLID, DRY, KISS, SRP, Clean Code.
- Preserve App Router, RSC/client boundaries, server actions per Next.js 16 + React 19 best practices.
- Mock/repository services scoped to feature; preserve **next-intl** and `/[locale]` routes.

## Tests

- Touch logic, filters, permissions, mocks, critical routes, or interaction → add/update unit/integration/E2E when it makes sense.
- Green tests ≠ pass if naming, styling, scope, or architecture are broken.

## Hydro / government context

- Read product & flow docs before inventing UX (`docs/product/`, `docs/product/flows/`).
- Consider: hidrovias Norte, Arco Norte, Amazonas-Solimões, Madeira, Tapajós, Tocantins-Araguaia; portos/IP4/TUP/ETC; ANTAQ; Marinha/NORMAM; Ibama; Receita/PF/Anvisa/MAPA/Vigiagro; Conportos; fiscalização; documentos; ETA; calado; seca; sazonalidade; riscos/gargalos.
- Reuse existing components/tokens before creating new ones.

## Official docs

- New Next.js/React architecture decisions → consult current official docs when online.
- No internet → state limitation; use local ADRs/project docs — do not fake verification.

## Output

- **Captain closeout first** in the closing section (≤3 lines in human checkpoint); technical proof after.
- Run mandatory `npm run hydri:gate` before closeout. **Any FAIL → 🔴 max** — never 🟢 or "Pode seguir". **Any WARN → 🟡 max**.
- Governance-only work on a dirty branch: 🔴 with *"Governança criada, mas branch atual segue bloqueada por FAIL legítimo no gate."* when product FAILs remain.
- Try automated preview/screenshot before asking the user; if automation fails → gate/closeout **WARN** path, not 🟢.
